==Strategy==
The fight against Darvin will be a difficult one. Having an extremely high amount of health, enough range to hit units like Newtone and Dr. Nova, and his Curse + Drain severely affecting your meatshielding, you will need to either clip Awakened Bahamut into his hitbox, or upgrade [[Ototo Corps#Foundation and Style Upgrades|Cat Base Foundations]] for a decent enough clear without any Ubers. For a no-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] strategy, clipping Bahamut is probably the easier method to do, especially since it's much easier to control and get one to two Knockbacks off against Darvin. (See the Walkthrough section for a Bahamut clip guide.)

While Darvin alone wouldn't be much of a problem, he comes assisted with infinite Boraphims and Commander Ostromedas, which severely restricts your lineup building. At the start, try to farm as many Mistress Celeboodles as possible with a [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|Money Up unit]], and then for the remainder of the battle cycle your [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] as quickly as possible to kill the supporting enemies fast. [[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|Sage Slayers]] have 70% resistance to Darvin's Drain, but the effect is still large enough that you should try to get as much stage length as possible to stall for your second set of Mythics. Newtone should be sent prematurely if you are doing the Bahamut clip strategy due to his speed, then Nova afterwards. Try to get Soractes spawned before Boraphim spawns to get him off cooldown quicker.

Try to eliminate Darvin before the second Boraphim spawns or there won't be enough ground to keep the fight going.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut is vital here to get damage off on Boraphim or Darvin early, even if he dies quickly. Additionally, if you time the [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] powerup, you can get Bahamut to clip into Darvin's hitbox where he can freely tear away at Darvin while avoiding all of Darvin's attacks for a while. Turn the Sniper off around when Darvin spawns, then turn it back on around when Bahamut is reaching Darvin.
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]]: Soractes having very high crowd-control potential against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] makes him extremely good for the Boraphim alongside a Conjure that can prevent Boraphim from breaking through your defenses for a bit.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Newtone]]: Newtone is practically mandatory here as the best way to deal damage to Ostromeda and Darvin. While Newtone will get chipped by Darvin and eventually die, his damage is too good to not bring him along here.
*[[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Master of Life Dr. Nova]]: Nova is highly recommended for no-Uber clears of this stage given her Slow, which is extremely important to stall Ostromeda. Nova will also be chipped by Darvin, but like Newtone you will have to risk that to try and win. Beware of Zackie Peng unburrows, as they will remove huge amounts of her health fast if they unburrow on top of her.
*[[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]]: Jiangshi being able to live two hits makes it the best meatshield to use here, as well as having an Attack [[Cat Combo|Combo]] with [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]], whom you might as well bring along anyways since it outranges Ostromeda.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Ramen will be needed here to stall Boraphim alongside Soractes support. You won't need Curse Resist since Darvin's damage is too high for it to matter.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Don't rely on Jelly Dumpling to get direct hits on Darvin. Instead, use it to deal with Thrillerz and Dogensteins.
*[[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Kinjirou Cat]]: Kinjirou's mobility and effective health makes it very useful to deal with stalling Ostromeda.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: If you own Cafeteria, you can replace Soractes with it. Cafeteria doesn't bring any meaningful CC, but does inflict Massive Damage to Angels. Being more spammable than Soractes and also being not quite as cash draining, Cafeteria's damage can rack up on Boraphim a lot quicker than you'd think.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: You will want to remove the Zackie Pengs, Dogensteins, and Gabriels as quickly as possible, so run Can Can like any other stage. Getting Money Up kills on Mistress Celeboodle is also vital to get your Legend units out quickly.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Can be used along side super-backliners like Master of Logic Newtone to be used to stall Ostromeda longer.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[The White Rabbit (Uber Rare Cat)|The Spectral Cat]]: One of the best Ubers against Darvin. Strong Against keeps her alive for longer while doing more damage, Sage Slayer does the same thing while allowing her debuffs to stick and reduces the effectiveness of Darvin's Drain ability, and those aforementioned debuffs allow for your cats to last longer in the face of Darvin. She also has Curse Immunity and Warp Immunity, so Darvin and Ostromeda can't throw her for a loop with their debuffs. She stands in Darvin's second hit to take reduced damage as well. She doesn't counter the other enemies here nearly as well, but if you have this [[Ultra Form]] then by all means use her.
*[[Mizli (Uber Rare Cat)|Mizunade]]: Fantastic source of DPS, and especially crowd-control, against the various Alien threats here. Darvin is practically unable to kill it, and it makes handling Ostromeda a far less arduous task if you lack Dr. Nova. You need to protect it during the Boraphim phases of the fight, however.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Bad Blaster Saki]]: Can deal large amounts of damage against both Darvin and Ostromeda. Her [[True Form]] is immune to Darvin's Curse, and with her Strong Against Talent she can take multiple hits from him without dying. She works great with Newtone, as his Conjure can push back enemies out of her blind spot allowing her to land more hits. However, be wary of both Zackie Peng and Boraphim who are able to easily enter her blind spot.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Thunder Jack can push Darvin back while he's alone, allowing you to regain large amounts of space which helps ease the pressure of the Ostromeda and Boraphim phases of the fight.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: A spammable attacker who can deal massive amounts of damage to Boraphim, outrange and chip down Ostromeda, and can act as an extra layer of defense due to his ranged meatshield properties which is especially important due to Darvin's Drain disrupting your meatshields.
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]]: Works great as an anti-Alien tanker who isn't worried about Darvin's Curse due to its Curse Immumity Talent, greatly helping out during the Ostromeda phases. Beware of Boraphim who will shred through Gravolodon's health in an instant however.
*[[Queen Reika (Uber Rare Cat)|Eternal Reika]]: Reika can dish out huge damage to Ostromeda and even Darvin himself if her Curse Immunity Talent is invested, while also capable of Zombie Killing Zackie Peng and Thrillerz for cash. However she can easily get juggled from Darvin's 2nd multi-hit which interrupts her from quickly killing Ostromeda.
*[[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Ushiwakamaru]]: Ushiwakamaru is capable of dealing 25,596 DPS towards Boraphim at Lv.50, and work as a generalist spammable unit like Kasa Jizo to deal with peons. However his low health against non-Angels makes him ideal for dealing with Boraphim only.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Supernova Cosmo has exceptional range as a Sage Slayer allowing him to chip both Darvin and Ostromeda from a safe distance. If one manages to keep him alive long enough, he will also be able to crowd-control Boraphim.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: His sheer burst damage potential is worth considering if more fitting Uber options are unavailable. His Multi-Hit's range turns out to be just perfect for hitting a melee pusher and a midrange threat at once, in this case Ostromeda/Boraphim and Darvin. With some luck, he can also eliminate an incoming Zackie Peng with his third Multi-Hit. Just like other heavy-hitters, do not expect him to stay for a very long time, but used wisely and he can bail you out of any situation.
*[[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Catman Forever]]: Deals very high damage and targets every main threat from a good range while his Drain Immunity blocks Darvin from increasing his cooldown. In short, he is a hard counter to this stage, perhaps worth getting purely for it.

